{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on d46cf7cf: the caller supplies the key of a fieldless offer.\n\nConfirmed, with four conditions.\n\n1. Describe allocates no key, retains no step and writes no store. It\n   has no key generator. In step E3 the local instance is the caller,\n   and the instance chooses the key.\n2. The key and the checked context travel together. A call with both\n   gets, for each kind, the template and, for a fieldless act, one\n   exploration. A call with neither gets the templates and no\n   exploration. A call with only one of the two throws TypeError.\n   Template code reads no context.\n3. One call uses its one key for each fieldless alternative. Each\n   alternative has its own version, the digest of its bound act as\n   written. So each alternative is a distinct Source, as the earlier\n   ruling on versions of one key says.\n4. Each alternative passes through actExplore with no special case.\n   The rules for assumes, owners, pending outputs and the unavailable\n   answers apply as ruled. Describe adds no Lack and no result form.\n\nE1 does not rule on the key that a later submit uses. A page can\nsubmit the chosen act under the same key, and its Source then equals\nthe Source of the exploration. E3 decides that rule for the instance.\n\nName one case for a fieldless act that is refused before the click,\nwith its guard reason, and one case for the call with no key. I add\nthis ruling to section 5.5 of the note in the amendment after E1.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}